4% in 2005 and should expand another 5% this year, Treasury said. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation allowed the country to contain inflation and limit interest rate hikes, while domestic demand strengthened, Treasury said.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia has a tightly managed exchange rate and domestic investment has been very weak, Treasury said. Singapore's current account surplus appears to be the product of high savings rates in a rapidly aging population. Russia's current account surplus has been bloated by oil exports, however, the real value of the ruble has appreciated sharply because of rapid inflation, Treasury said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Elizabeth Price, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9295; Elizabeth.Price@dowjones.com\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 05-10-06 1600ET  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060510e25a002pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
