\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Yuan Ends Down On OTC;PBOC Suspected Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2006\par 10:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan closed lower against the U.S. dollar on the over-the-counter market Wednesday, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure two-way movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 On the over-the-counter market the dollar was at CNY8.0084 at 0730 GMT, after trading in a range of CNY8.0105 and CNY8.0071. It closed at CNY8.0050 Tuesday, below the automatic price-matching system level of CNY8.0099.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the U.S. dollar closed Wednesday at CNY8.0072 on the automatic price-matching system after trading in a range of CNY8.0075 to CNY8.0070.  \par \par \uc2 The central parity was set at 8.0120.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they were surprised the central parity was set so high a week ahead of President Hu Jintao's visit to the U.S., and after the dollar weakened against the euro and yen overnight.  \par \par \uc2 Although the yuan doesn't always track international markets, dealers said the yuan usually appreciates when the dollar falls overseas.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have played a role in keeping the rate high.  \par \par \uc2 "This might be part of efforts to introduce more volatility in the market...for the yuan not to just move in one direction," said a Shenzhen-based dealer with a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it intends to introduce more two-way movement in the rate.  \par \par \uc2 A Shanghai-based dealer with a foreign bank agreed the bank was likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "There were very large bids at 8.0070 and 8.0065 (on the OTC market) that could be the work of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said. "It would be very difficult for the rate to fall below this level."  \par \par \uc2 The offshore bid/offer quote for the one-year dollar-yuan nondeliverable forward was 7.6920/7.6920, down a little from 7.6930/7.6950 late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The one-year is at a fairly stable level for now," said a Hong Kong-based trader. "The market is not convinced the dollar will fall below CNY7.70 in a year."  \par \par \uc2 The trader said speculation Hu's visit to the U.S. next week will bring concessions on the yuan is unlikely to push 1-year NDFs down any further. 1-year NDFs have fallen since the end of March, when they were trading above 7.7400.  \par \par \uc2 -By Denis McMahon, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6120-1200; denis.mcmahon\u174\'00\'AEdowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by David Riordan [ 12-04-06 0828GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060412e24c000di\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
