\par\par \b \uc2 CHINA PRESS:China End-Jan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves $845.2B; Up $26.8B  \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 06:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to $845.2 billion at the end of January, up $26.8 billion from the end of December, the China Securities Journal reported Wednesday, citing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.  \par \par \uc2 The reported monthly rise would be the largest increase in China's reserves since December 2004 and indicate added pressure on China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, to rise.  \par \par \uc2 The faster growth in China's January reserves mirrors the trend in the rest of Asia, where reserves grew by about $30 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially reports its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on a quarterly basis.  \par \par \uc2 China's growing reserves indicate the extent \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to counteract appreciation pressure on the yuan. Upward pressure on the yuan's value is driven by China's trade surplus, foreign investment, and hot money inflows. The USD/CNY was up slightly midday at 8.0483 from 8.0481 at Wednesday's close on the automatic price-matching system.  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are the second-largest in the world, trailing only Japan. Japan held $850.06 billion in reserves at the end of February, down $1.61 billion from January.  \par \par \