\par\par \b \uc2 China Yuan Ends Up, Hits Another Post-Revaluation High  \b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2006\par 09:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan ended slightly higher Tuesday, but off a post-revaluation high hit early in the session, and traders said further rises would depend on whether or not the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar closed at CNY8.0402 on the automatic price matching system after trading in a range of CNY8.0405 and CNY8.0397, a post-revaluation low. It closed at 8.0407 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 On the over-the-counter market, the dollar was at CNY8.0404 at 0731 GMT. It traded between CNY8.0409 and CNY8.0402.  \par \par \uc2 There was strong support for the dollar at the psychological CNY8.0400 level, and traders, who expected that level to be breached easily Tuesday, said the market would close below CNY8.04 when the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped its dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "I think later this week or early next week the 8.04 could be tested," said a trader at a market-maker bank. "The key is to watch for the fixing rate. When that rate falls below 8.04, the rate will fall," he said, referring to the central parity rate set each morning.  \par \par \uc2 Comments by a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulatory official that China aims to achieve basic capital account convertibility in the near future, but that total convertibility is a long term goal, had little impact on the market.  \par \par \uc2 "We need to maintain a general balance of capital outflows and inflows," said Zou Lin, director of the capital account department at the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We actively encourage outflows," said Zou, who made his remarks at a local investment conference.  \par \par \uc2 "Those moves would reduce the appreciation pressure, but they won't change the fact the yuan will rise 5% this year (against the dollar)," said a trader at a foreign bank in Shanghai.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the offshore dollar/yuan nondeliverable forwards rose slightly on traders' disappointment onshore rates fell less than expected, said a trader in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year NDFs rose 0.0030 to 7.6980 by late afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 In other spot trading pairs, the Hong Kong dollar ended up at CNY1.0362 from CNY1.0360; the Japanese yen ended down at CNY6.9130 per 100 yen from CNY6.9200; and the euro ended higher at CNY9.5400 from CNY9.5300.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jane Lanhee Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6120-1200; jane.lee@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Theresa Davidovitz [ 28-02-06 0810GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060228e22s000ds\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
