\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China allows yuan to rise to new high  \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2006\par 02:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds market close, dealers' comments)  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Feb 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan ended at its highest level to the dollar since its revaluation in July as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed out of the market and let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate steadily but slowly, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan <CNY=CFXS> finished at 8.0545, its strongest closing level since Beijing revalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2.1 percent in July. It also set a post-revaluation intraday high of 8.0535 in early trade on Wednesday, up from Tuesday's close of 8.0566.  \par \par \uc2 "The trend will continue of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowing the yuan to go up gradually, though at a controlled pace," said a dealer at a major Chinese commercial bank.  \par \par \uc2 "Dealers know how to cope with the status quo," he said. "They will not push the yuan to rise too quickly, too sharply because that will trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The yuan weakened to 6.8270 versus 100 yen from Tuesday's 6.7830 after the yen gained versus the dollar on global markets.  \par \par \uc2 Several dealers forecast the yuan would rise above the new benchmark level of 8.05 against the dollar within two weeks of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breaking through the key 8.06 level.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  encouraged gains in the yuan when it announced an unexpectedly strong mid-point for the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning, allowing the yuan to stand firmly above the 8.06 level since then.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's close matched the daily mid-point of the yuan set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yuan can theoretically rise or fall 0.3 percent from its mid-point during the day, though it only moves a fraction of the range for most days.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they would wait for hints from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on possible movements in the yuan's exchange rates, while there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Wednesday trading.  \par \par \uc2 Though the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now allowing the yuan to appreciate gradually, it has a strong grip on the pace of its future gains, dealers said. By Wednesday's close, the yuan had appreciated only 0.69 percent since the July policy change.  \par \par \uc2 One-year onshore yuan forwards were traded at 7.8100 to the dollar by 0909 GMT on Wednesday, anticipating the yuan would be 3.1 percent stronger in one year's time.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan closed firmer to 9.6400 to the euro from 9.6500.  \par \par \uc2 The exchange-traded market closes at 0730 GMT, but the yuan's over-the-counter trading continues until 0930 GMT. More information on OTC trade can be seen on the exchange's Web site ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn }}}\uc2 ).  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Z|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060208e2280002w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
