\par\par \b \uc2 China Official: Full CNY Convertibility In Future-Xinhua  \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2006\par 04:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--China's long-term goal is to make the yuan fully convertible, the official Xinhua News Agency reported Thursday, citing a senior Chinese official.  \par \par \uc2 "Our goal is to make the renminbi float, but it will take some time," said Cheng Siwei, vice chairman of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress.  \par \par \uc2 "The renminbi will be fully convertible in the future," Cheng was quoted in the report as saying. The renminbi is another term for the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 Cheng made his remarks at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland. [ 26-01-06 0402GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Cheng also said China would like to bring down its growth rate as part of a more sustainable development.  \par \par \uc2 "We would like to lower our growth rate to 8% if possible and to devote more energy to social progress," Cheng said. "We can keep a relatively high growth rate but not as high as the double digits."  \par \par \uc2 The report cited Cheng as saying China may set a moderate growth rate of 8% in the next five years, and the country's main challenges include dealing with resource and environmental constraints, evening out regional and rural-urban development, and alleviating poverty.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday, China said its economy expanded 9.9% in 2005, slowing just slightly from the 10.1% recorded for 2004 and 10% in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 In China's latest Five-Year Plan for 2006-2010, policy makers have said they continue to aim for the full convertibility of the yuan, which remains tightly controlled under the capital account.  \par \par \uc2 Beijing moved to a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime in July when it revalued the yuan 2.1% against the dollar, and broke its effective dollar peg to begin referencing its value to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the local unit still trades very narrowly because of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Five-Year Plan, to be endorsed by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largely rubber-stamp legislature, the NPC, is expected to focus on agriculture and energy.  \par \par \uc2 China's rapid economic growth has resulted in energy bottlenecks and over-investment in some pockets of the economy like steel and autos. Beijing has been aiming its macro-economic controls at rebalancing growth to a more sustainable structure.  \par \par \uc2 The NPC's annual session begins March 5.  \par \par \uc2 -By J.R. Wu, Dow Jones Newswires; 8610 6588-5848; jr.wu@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by David Riordan [ 26-01-06 0435GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060126e21q0003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
