\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan falls as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen capping any rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2006\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Jan 25 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened marginally versus the dollar on Wednesday ahead of a week-long holiday, as speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week sapped optimism that it would be allowed to rise quickly.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan <CNY=CFXS> ended at 8.0619 per dollar, weaker than Tuesday's close of 8.0614.  \par \par \uc2 "There were signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the day before yesterday, especially that afternoon, as the yuan approached the 8.06 mark," said a dealer at a major foreign bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Round figures often spur \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Today's trajectory was partly due to Monday, and many banks are in holiday mood."  \par \par \uc2 Strength in the U.S. dollar, which had stabilised after Tuesday's jump, also kept the yuan range-bound, said the dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan has appreciated by just short of 0.6 percent against the dollar since Beijing revalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2.1 percent on July 21 and dropped its peg to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the yuan's recent strength had reflected demand from Chinese companies which are withdrawing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to award New Year's bonuses.  \par \par \uc2 The short-term outlook is for a gradual rise against the dollar, although dealers expect further People's Bank of China adjustments as the yuan approaches key values versus the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 One-year onshore yuan forwards were quoted at 7.81 to the dollar on Wednesday, anticipating the yuan would be 3.2 percent stronger in a year's time. Three deals were done, but none of them were for a whole year.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan closed at 9.9000 against the euro, unchanged from Tuesday. It ended at 7.0010 versus 100 Japanese yen from 7.0350 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|Z|E|RBN|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060125e21p000o3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
