\par\par \b \uc2 2ND UPDATE: China Adopts Over-the-counter Trading For Yuan  \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2006\par 14:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 By Chris Oliver  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones) -- China will allow its domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be traded over the counter in the interbank spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from Wednesday, the People's Bank of China said on a statement on its Web site.  \par \par \uc2 The measures will enhance the PBoC's flexibility in managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while reducing the need for daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said HSBC's chief \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist, Qu Hong.  \par \par \uc2 The move will not affect the yuan exchange rate. Also remaining in place is the trading band, which limits the yuan's rise or fall against foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 0.3% in any single day of trading.  \par \par \uc2 "By removing the crawling element in the formation of the central parity rate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be more capable of managing the pace of appreciation, while introducing greater daily volatility into the yuan's exchange rates," Qu said.  \par \par \uc2 As part of the change, China will publish benchmark rates each trading day against the U.S. dollar, the euro, yen and Hong Kong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The new system means the benchmark rate will no longer be based on the closing prices of the previous day. Instead, the benchmark will be calculated using a weighted average of market opening bid prices. Weightings will be determined by a formula that looks at the volumes of respective market makers as well as other factors.  \par \par \uc2 "Such a change will remove the crawling mechanism from the yuan's new regime introduced in July of 2005," Qu said.  \par \par \uc2 HSBC forecasts the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rise 2.7% to 7.85 yuan to the U.S. dollar by the end of year.  \par \par \uc2 The PBoC said the move is in line with international standards, and will help lower trading costs and diversify credit risk.  \par \par \uc2 In 2004, volume on China's interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reached $290 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "Along with the increase in trading volumes and in market participants, demand for transactions and risk management has diversified day by day and the introduction of OTC has become an objective necessity," the PBoC statement said. [ 01-03-06 0820ET ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020060103e21300009\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
