ed to push China for more flexibility over its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime during his trip to Beijing later this month, a trader in Hong Kong said.  \par \par \uc2 Onshore, Industrial & Commercial Bank of China posted a one-year forward price of 780.39 per 100 dollars on its Web site Wednesday morning, compared with 781.19 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 There were five dollar/yuan forwards transactions on the onshore market: a 273-day deal at 7.8785, a 16-day deal at 8.0725, a 93-day deal at 8.0235, a 172-day deal at 7.9755 and a 364-day deal at 7.8120, the Chinamoney Web site shows.  \par \par \uc2 In other pairs, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0420, down from CNY1.0425; the Japanese yen rose to CNY6.8852 per 100 yen from CNY6.8548; and the euro ended at CNY9.5091, up from CNY9.4641.  \par \par \uc2 -Sun Yan contributed to this story; Dow Jones Newswires; 8621 6120-1200; yan.sun@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Sharon Buan  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020051109e1b9006k5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
