\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 3-China widens non-dlr yuan bands  \b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2005\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 23 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday widened the daily permitted trading band for the yuan <CNY=CFXS> against non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 3.0 percent from 1.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The news sparked initial dollar sales, boosting the yen and euro, although analysts said the move did not amount to a policy shift.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said banks, in dealings with customers, could now set their own bid/ask spreads in trading the yuan, or renminbi, against non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It also widened the bid/ask spread banks are permitted to quote in dollar deals for clients.  \par \par \uc2 Following are reactions from analysts to the news.  \par \par \uc2 DAVID SIMMONDS, HEAD OF \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESEARCH, ROYAL BANK OF SCOTLAND, LONDON:  \par \par \uc2 "It is technical adjustment to existing policy, not another policy change."  \par \par \uc2 "Clearly their overriding priority is to maintain control of the dollar/China exchange rate and therefore, in the move announced today, they are ensuring that if we did see sharper day-to-day moves in euro/dollar or dollar/yen, they are allowing more of that heat to be reflected in bigger moves in euro/China or in China/yen than they previously allowed.  \par \par \uc2 "So, it is cutting themselves a bit more slack and reducing the risk that they be drawn into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to maintain the credibility of the dollar/China and non-dollar/China fluctuation ranges."  \par \par \uc2 SEAN CALLOW, SENIOR \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, WESTPAC INSTITUTIONAL BANK, SINGAPORE:  \par \par \uc2 "China's decision to widen the daily trading bands against its non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is effectively just accepting the inevitable -- that the likes of euro and yen can fluctuate by more than 1.5 percent vs dollar in an given day, so that the PBOC should not try to guarantee renminbi's value against them.  \par \par \uc2 "The timing of this move -- just hours before China's top officials meet with their US counterparts in Washington, DC -- is presumably designed to cool criticism over the lack of flexibility in renminbi trade."  \par \par \uc2 MIRZA BAIG, \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, DEUTSCHE BANK, SINGAPORE:  \par \par \uc2 "It makes no difference. It is a red herring."  \par \par \uc2 "China had fixed the trading ranges. This is China giving up and saying forget it.  \par \par \uc2 "The trading band which was 1.5 percent for euro/yuan earlier would have meant that \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/dollar and dollar/yuan to limit volatility around euro/yuan.  \par \par \uc2 "They have doubled that to suggest that euro/china has to move by 3.3 percent before they come in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "But they never actually did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in the 1.8 percent band. I don't think they would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now.  \par \par \uc2 "Also, nobody cares in terms of traders and brokers. The market is ignoring the move."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-CHINA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -VIEW (UPDATE2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|O|OIL|UKI|U|NAT|ABX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050923e19n000no\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
