 \uc2 Indonesia's pending \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap deal with China follows Burhanuddin's announcement in Tokyo Wednesday of a second bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps of up to $6 billion between monetary authorities in Indonesia and Japan.  \par \par \uc2 That pact also increased to 20% from 10% the percentage of a swap line available without an International Monetary Fund economic reform agreement or being close to reaching such an IMF agreement.  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia ended its IMF program at the end of 2004. -By Jakarta Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; dj.jakarta@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050901e191007y6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
