\par\par \b \uc2 China Yuan Ends Slightly Up; Market Cautious Near 8.1000  \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2005\par 10:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan closed higher against the U.S. dollar Thursday, after traders became cautious as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair approached the 8.1000 support.  \par \par \uc2 In the onshore spot market, the U.S. dollar ended down at CNY8.1002, after trading between CNY8.1006 and CNY8.1002, the tightest trading range since July 21's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime change. It closed at CNY8.1005 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 A Shenzhen dealer said market participants turned cautious near CNY8.1000, a key psychological support, as \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the 8.1000 level is breached.  \par \par \uc2 Since the initial 2.1% revaluation against the dollar last month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan has never neared the 0.3% daily movement that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it permits against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The offshore bid/offer quote for one-year dollar/yuan nondeliverable forwards was 7.8390/7.8490, down from 7.8500/7.8600 late Wednesday, in line with the dollar's decline in the spot market.  \par \par \uc2 Opinions in the market are mixed on the direction of the yuan in the next 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 Some market participants are expecting a 4% to 5% appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a year, said a Hong Kong trader.  \par \par \uc2 But ING Barings chief economist for Asia ex-Japan Tim Condon said "at the current rate of appreciation, we are unlikely to see any yuan strengthening in a year."  \par \par \uc2 The recent rangebound movement of the NDF "is a reflection of the minimal spot rate movement," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Onshore, Industrial & Commercial Bank of China posted one-year forwards prices on its Web site Thursday morning at 785.71 per 100 dollars, up from 784.24 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 In other spot trading pairs, the Hong Kong dollar ended up at CNY1.0420 from CNY1.0418; the Japanese yen rose to CNY7.3709 per 100 yen from CNY7.3235; and the euro rose to CNY9.9661 from CNY9.8721. Thursday's larger euro and yen movements didn't affect the dollar/yuan pair, said dealers.  \par \par \uc2 -By Daniel Pescatore, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; daniel.pescatore@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by David Riordan [ 25-08-05 0831GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050825e18p000fj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
