\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan weakens as cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2005\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, dealer comments)  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Aug 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan <CNY=CFXS> weakened on Tuesday after closing at a post-revaluation high of 8.0971 in the previous session, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening too sharply.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan closed at 8.1002 to the dollar. It was revalued by 2.1 percent on July 21 to 8.11, and is now 0.12 percent firmer -- not much by the standards of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but much more than the infinitesimal moves allowed before the policy change.  \par \par \uc2 Still, dealers expected the yuan to firm slowly but steadily over the rest of this week, but see resistance at 8.0900.  \par \par \uc2 "There were obvious signs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down today," said a trader at a major Chinese bank in Shanghai. "But the yuan is likely to resume its upward move later in the week."  \par \par \uc2 "Unless there is more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which I don't think will happen, the yuan will keep strengthening this week," said a dealer at another Chinese bank in the southern city of Shenzhen.  \par \par \uc2 "That's the trend that's being set."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to strengthen or weaken by 0.3 percent daily, though it has yet to come even close to using up that leeway.  \par \par \uc2 Despite such miniscule daily moves, dealers said the revaluation had aggravated \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks for financial institutions -- from banks and trust firms to rural credit cooperatives -- and welcomed the launch of hedging instruments on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 China kicked off trade in onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards this week, which signal domestic expectations for how much the yuan might appreciate in up to a year's time.  \par \par \uc2 Prior to the move, the government allowed only a small number of players, including state-owned Bank of China and the Industrial and Commercial Bank of China [ICBC.UL], to settle \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards for local corporate clients.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan ended softer against the yen at 7.4297 on Tuesday but firmed against the euro to 10.0035 from 10.0535.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-CLOSE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|Z|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050816e18g000lm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
