\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Yuan Up Midday;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected  \b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2005\par 07:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan was up against the dollar shortly after midday Friday, but came back slightly after opening at its highest level since the revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early to bring the yuan lower, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday hit a post-revaluation high for the closing level.  \par \par \uc2 Onshore trading of the U.S. dollar was down at CNY8.0996 against the yuan, versus Thursday's close of CNY8.1002, after trading between CNY8.0995 and CNY8.1005.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan rose strongly Thursday, tracking gains in the Japanese yen and the euro against the dollar, onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 However, after opening strongly Friday at CNY8.0995, the yuan crept back a little through the morning session.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was almost certainly active in the market this morning," said a Shanghai-based trader at a non-Chinese bank, who added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably uncomfortable with Thursday's fairly large trading range. He said he expected trading in the afternoon to stay in the same range as in the morning session.  \par \par \uc2 Thursday, the yuan traded between CNY8.1045 and CNY8.1002 against the dollar. It was the first time the trading band has widened since Aug. 3. [ 12-08-05 0512GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The yuan's de facto peg to the dollar was scrapped in July, in favor of a managed float that references the yuan to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Wednesday, People's Bank of China Governor Zhou Xiaochuan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is weighted mostly to the U.S. dollar, euro, Japanese yen and Korean won.  \par \par \uc2 Nondeliverable forwards prices continued to come back slightly after they converged with onshore forwards prices following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards reform.  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened participation in onshore forwards trading to more banks, and the following day it launched \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards trading on the interbank market.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the market had overshot and prices had since come back a little.  \par \par \uc2 The offshore bid/offer quote for one-year USD/CNY NDFs was 7.8100/7.8175, down from 7.8220/7.8280 late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Onshore, Industrial & Commercial Bank of China posted bid/offer prices for one-year forwards on its Web site Friday morning at 777.03/783.27 per 100 dollars, down from 777.6/783.85 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 A Hong Kong-based trader said that prices were also falling because of speculation that the yuan might be revalued again before the end of the year. He said that recent comments from George Soros, which tipped the yuan to rise another 1% to 2% as soon as September, contributed to the NDF selling.  \par \par \uc2 The trader said he expects one-year NDF prices to fall to a mid price of 7.7780 over the coming weeks before settling.  \par \par \uc2 In other spot trading pairs, the Hong Kong dollar was flat at CNY1.0420 around midday, the Japanese yen rose to CNY7.3711 per 100 yen from CNY7.3395, and the euro rose to CNY10.0850 from CNY10.0455.  \par \par \uc2 -By Denis McMahon, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6120-1200; denis.mcmahon@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by David Riordan [ 12-08-05 0536GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050812e18c0005v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
