\par\par \b \uc2 China yuan forwards steady as c.bank curbs strength  \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2005\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 1 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan forwards market was little changed on Monday as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength kept traders from betting on further gains in the managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month non-deliverable yuan forward contract <CNYNDF=>, which foreign investors use to bet on the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value in the near term, edged up to 8.0850 per dollar from 8.0870 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year forward contract used to speculate on the longer-term value of the yuan was quoted at 7.7550 per dollar, also up only marginally from 7.7575 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "It's barely moving. The Chinese are holding the spot," said a Singapore-based yuan NDF trader, referring to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the spot exchannge rate from strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan <CNY=CFXS> traded on Monday at 8.1054 per dollar, little changed from Friday's closing rate of 8.1056.  \par \par \uc2 Operators in the yuan forward market have scaled back their bets on a sharper appreciation in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term after local trading showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reluctant to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain significantly after the country ended its peg of 8.28 per dollar on July 21.  \par \par \uc2 Although the yuan is allowed to gain or weaken by as much as 0.3 percent against the dollar each day under the new regime, it has risen only 0.06 percent over the past seven trading sessions after the initial 2.1 percent revaluation to 8.11 per dollar on July 21.  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Zhou Xiaochuan, said in a statement on Friday that recent trading in the yuan after the revaluation showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value reflected supply and demand as well as moves in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ((Editing by Alan Raybould; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging: rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3841))  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-YUAN-NDF|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|Z|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050801e1810005m\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (china near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\